<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINE COSTANERA Q2 NET $14.3 MLN VS $10.5 MLN.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINE COSTANERA Q2 NET $14.3 MLN VS $10.5 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to June 30. Net $14.3 million vs $10.5 million Revs $80.09 million vs $75.96 million  </p>
<p>1st-half</p>
<p>EPS $0.22 VS $0.19</p>
<p>ADR $2.2 VS $1.9</p>
<p>Revs $166.4 million vs $161.8 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Central Costanera SA provided no EPS or ADR for the second quarter. The controlling 51 percent stake in Costanera is owned by Chile's ENDESA, which in turn is controlled by Chile's ENERSIS SA.</p>
<p>At June 30 Costanera's net worth stood at $361.5 million.</p>
<p>Costanera is one of the country's two biggest thermoelectric generating companies, the other being Central Puerto SA, run by Chile's Chilgener SA.</p>
<p>((-Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
</text>
